# ==============================
# SPELL NAMES AND DESCRIPTIONS
# ==============================
# A spell's name and description live here, not in spells/<id>.yml. Each spell owns one
# block keyed by its id with the underscores removed, so fire_blast and earth_spike are
# spells.fireblast.* and spells.earthspike.*.
#
# This file shadows the copy bundled in the jar, so edit it freely and run
# /alkatraz reload to apply it. Do not delete it: the bundled copy is written back on
# the next server start and any edits go with it.
#
# Colour codes: &a and friends for the legacy codes, #RRGGBB for hex. A hex code carries
# no ampersand in front of it - &#RRGGBB is not a valid form in a lang file and leaves a
# stray & in the output. See spells.earthspike.name further up for a hex example.
#
# A value is a single line. This format has no line continuations, so a value wrapped
# across two physical lines is silently cut at the break. Use the two characters
# backslash and n to make a description span several lines, and repeat the colour code
# on every segment:
#   spells.fireball.description = &7A small ball of fire that can be shot\n&7at an enemy.
#
# Every spell's real .name and .description keys sit in that spell's own block further up
# this file; the line above only shows the shape. spells.<prefix>.book_name is a
# different string - the title of the book the spell is learned from - and neither it nor
# the name comes from the spell's yml any more.

# ==============================
# RESEARCH OVERRIDES (optional)
# ==============================
# research.yml nodes and categories can be renamed from here. Uncomment or add keys.
# Format: override.research.<type>.<id>.<field>
# ==============================
# override.research.nodes.<id>.name = &aCustom Name
# override.research.nodes.<id>.description = &7Custom description line 1\nCustom description line 2
# override.research.categories.<id>.name = &aCustom Category Name
